The root cause of the bug is that when `Get` finds a key in the `recent` cache, it promotes the key to the `frequent` cache but fails to remove it from `recent`. This causes the key to exist in both maps, leading to inflated counts reported by `Len()` and elements duplicated in `Keys()`.

I will modify the `Get` method in `2q.go` to ensure that when a hit occurs in `recent`, the key is first removed from `recent` before being added to `frequent`.

